# DemWatch rules

Source of truth: `docs/preferences.md` (Project preferences).

## Home / map
- No large DemWatch hero/banner on the home page.
- US map is the first content on the index.
- Newly elected ↔ Already in office control sits close to the map.
- Cohort toggle animation should feel smooth and fancy (not a bare cut).

## Roster coverage
- **Already in office** includes the full voting House Democratic Caucus, not a leadership subset.
- Document coverage; exclude non-voting delegates unless explicitly requested.

## Claims & Pursuing
- Every factual claim must be sourced (links on the claim).
- **Pursuing** = attributed hard goals (controversial statements, tweets/X, bills they said they want to do).
- Never use generic “continues serving” or party-framing filler.
- Leave Pursuing empty (“None yet”) if no attributed hard goal exists — do not invent.

## Controversy calendar
- Every official page has a dated controversy calendar (speeches, tweets/X, related news/trends).
- Each entry: date, short description, source link(s).
- No invented events; empty calendar OK when unsourced.
- Calendar data lives in `src/data/calendars.json` keyed by official id.

## UI copy
- No explanatory blurbs under module titles — headings only.
- Keep functional legends/controls.
- Empty states stay minimal (“None yet”).

## Monorepo
- Web app at repo root (Vite + React).
- `bots/` is reserved for a separate worker — do not invent bot code here.
